<h2>Where Byname differs</h2>
<p>These are facts about Byname, from the app and the docs.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Open source, and you run it.</strong> MIT licensed. One container and Postgres. Provided by Unkey. There is no seat price and no hosted plan.</li>
  <li><strong>Your keys.</strong> One Treg token runs the AI apps, or you bring your own provider keys and gateways, app by app. The bill comes from that provider.</li>
  <li><strong>What a check cost.</strong> One check on November 26, 2026 ran 390 answers and cost $2.96. The estimate for a check of that size every 3 days is $44.12 a month. See <a href="/cost">what Byname costs</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Several brands, one install.</strong> Each brand has its own questions, results, and MCP server. The team, the sign-in, and the provider keys are shared.</li>
  <li><strong>Search, social, and AI answers together.</strong> Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools stay on their own timelines. Byname also searches X, Reddit, Hacker News, LinkedIn, YouTube, Threads, and Bluesky for posts that name you.</li>
  <li><strong>Each AI app is labeled.</strong> Seven are read from the app a person uses. Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and Codex CLI are asked with your team's model and web search on, and labeled as the same model, not the full tool. The Claude app and the Perplexity app are stand-ins, and Byname says so.</li>
</ul>
